WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.496 --> 00:00:10.607
First of all, I'd like to ask
you a question.

00:00:10.607 --> 00:00:14.305
What is beauty?

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:18.697
Beauty is a single word, but we use it
to describe a billion different things.

00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:23.047
And it's this universal concept that
is totally subjective.

00:00:23.047 --> 00:00:26.228
How would you determine if something
else is beautiful?

00:00:26.228 --> 00:00:30.979
What does it mean 
when something isn't beautiful?

00:00:30.979 --> 00:00:32.388
Wait, where are my manners?

00:00:32.388 --> 00:00:34.448
A very good evening 
to the beautiful ladies

00:00:34.448 --> 00:00:36.358
and most certainly handsome gentlemen,

00:00:36.358 --> 00:00:37.488
fellow TED speakers,

00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:39.647
and everyone present today.

00:00:39.647 --> 00:00:43.870
Throughout our lives, we are surrounded
by a cacophony of noise

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.359
telling us what we should do,

00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:46.839
how we should act,

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:49.471
and who we should be.

00:00:49.471 --> 00:00:51.488
Not convinced?

00:00:51.488 --> 00:00:57.340
Long hair, a fair complexion, sexy eyes,
luscious lips, perky breasts,

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.330
a small waist, a flat stomach,
a shapely bum, long legs,

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.100
finally finishing with a symmetrical body

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.650
completes the ideal look of physically
perfect woman.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:13.782
However, if I were to tell you that these
stereotypes only apply to women,

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:19.470
I would be lying.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.324
His hair is a stylish chaos,

00:01:21.324 --> 00:01:23.391
the eyes, deep and captivating,

00:01:23.391 --> 00:01:25.482
the jawline, masculine and chiseled,

00:01:25.482 --> 00:01:31.862
broad shoulders, chest muscles, six-pack
abs, rippling biceps, a wide back,

00:01:31.862 --> 00:01:38.503
oh, and he must be six feet and above.

00:01:38.503 --> 00:01:41.953
From the broad chest of Superman
to the tiny waists of Disney princesses,

00:01:41.953 --> 00:01:45.163
our perception of beauty has been
so greatly influenced by the media

00:01:45.163 --> 00:01:52.043
that we subconsciously accept these 
requirements as being true and just.

00:01:52.043 --> 00:01:57.194
Therefore, nowadays people are boycotted, 
isolated, discriminated, even,

00:01:57.194 --> 00:02:01.994
because they are thought of as ugly,
or different, for that matter.

00:02:01.994 --> 00:02:04.604
And that's why in the pursuit of beauty,

00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:11.215
people tend to go overboard
and finally become something they're not.

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:13.936
Twelve years ago, The Swan took the world
by storm,

00:02:13.936 --> 00:02:18.286
being described as Jennifer Pozner as the
most sadistic reality show of the decade.

00:02:18.286 --> 00:02:22.275
Now, The Swan is a 2004 American reality
television program

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.264
in which women who were judged
to be ugly

00:02:24.264 --> 00:02:28.747
were given extreme makeovers
to fulfill their greatest fantasies.

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:32.576
Contestants collectively received more
than 4 million dollars worth of treatment

00:02:32.576 --> 00:02:35.477
including tummy tucks, 
breast augmentations,

00:02:35.477 --> 00:02:39.494
rhinoplasty, jaw and nose reconstruction,
laser hair removals,

00:02:39.494 --> 00:02:43.178
I'm just saying This is an extremely 
complicated and time-consuming process,

00:02:43.178 --> 00:02:46.557
not to mention the agonizing
physical pain

00:02:46.557 --> 00:02:52.738
these people have 
to endure over two months.

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:57.558
Some of them were happy.
That's good.

00:02:57.558 --> 00:03:01.448
But for some, relationships crumbled,

00:03:01.448 --> 00:03:03.438
some gained weight,

00:03:03.438 --> 00:03:06.740
some of them contemplated suicide,

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.238
and for some of them,
they still suffer

00:03:10.238 --> 00:03:16.089
from depression, agoraphobia,
and crippling mental disorders.

00:03:16.089 --> 00:03:18.970
This might seem staggering,
ladies and gentlemen,

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.580
yet thousands of individuals 
squealed in delight

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:29.832
when they were told that they
were chosen to become a Swan

00:03:29.832 --> 00:03:33.762
because they were sick of being
called ugly,

00:03:33.762 --> 00:03:38.920
they were sick of insecure marriages,

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:43.551
and this is the product of our
beauty-obsessed culture.

00:03:43.551 --> 00:03:46.351
Yet another blight that consumes
so many young people

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:47.751
is anorexia nervosa,

00:03:47.751 --> 00:03:50.841
an eating disorder that is characterized
by a fear of weight gain

00:03:50.841 --> 00:03:54.392
leading to malnutrition
or excessive weight loss.

00:03:54.392 --> 00:03:57.684
Kirsten Haglund was 19 when she became
Miss America in 2008,

00:03:57.684 --> 00:04:01.322
one of the youngest beauty queens
ever to win the national title.

00:04:01.322 --> 00:04:05.123
Yet, she was the victim of anorexia.

00:04:05.123 --> 00:04:08.614
She now uses this platform of her title
to raise awareness

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.272
about this very sensitive subject.

00:04:11.272 --> 00:04:15.234
She was struggling with this disturbing
disorder since the age of twelve.

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.213
Consuming fewer than 900 calories daily,

00:04:17.213 --> 00:04:20.104
less than half the recommended
for the average woman her age,

00:04:20.104 --> 00:04:24.345
she became obsessed with the need
to reduce her weight even further.

00:04:24.345 --> 00:04:27.694
Starving herself and adding even
more exercise to her regular routine

00:04:27.694 --> 00:04:29.044
and demanding schedule,

00:04:29.044 --> 00:04:33.464
she arrived to a nearly
irreversible condition.

00:04:33.464 --> 00:04:36.394
If not for the help of her mother
and multiple specialists,

00:04:36.394 --> 00:04:40.305
she would have reached a point
of no return.

00:04:40.305 --> 00:04:44.056
And all of this is for the sake of fitting
herself into the image of beauty,

00:04:44.056 --> 00:04:48.136
inculcated into her mind by the
questionable standards of our society.

00:04:48.136 --> 00:04:54.065
From time to time, I wonder.

00:04:54.065 --> 00:04:57.656
Why do we hold physical traits
with such high regard?

00:04:57.656 --> 00:05:08.419
Do we not realize that what's inside
is far more important?

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:12.147
I mean, you might have the gratification
of looking great,

00:05:12.147 --> 00:05:16.037
and you might have that satisfaction
of fitting into a smaller shirt,

00:05:16.037 --> 00:05:19.187
but besides showing that you've
changed your appearance,

00:05:19.187 --> 00:05:22.531
what else does that say about you?

00:05:22.531 --> 00:05:26.357
Now, let me show you 
guys something special,

00:05:26.357 --> 00:05:30.338
something you might not believe.

00:05:30.338 --> 00:05:37.720
So this is me when I was ten years old.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:41.249
As you can see, I was fat,
like really, really fat,

00:05:41.249 --> 00:05:42.409
but it didn't bother.

00:05:42.409 --> 00:05:45.039
I mean, I played tennis and badminton,
and everything,

00:05:45.039 --> 00:05:46.851
but man, I just loved eating.

00:05:46.851 --> 00:05:49.071
So I just ate and ate
and got fatter and fatter

00:05:49.071 --> 00:05:52.379
until I reached puberty,
when I just slimmed down all of a sudden.

00:05:52.379 --> 00:05:54.590
You see, I completely forgot
I looked like this

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:56.790
until one day I was going 
through old photos.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.350
I just went, "oh my goodness!"

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.651
I rushed to my mom, I said,

00:05:59.651 --> 00:06:04.590
"Mom, how could you let me
look like this?"

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:09.791
But she was puzzled and said,
"Look like what?"

00:06:09.791 --> 00:06:14.140
"This! This!"

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:20.521
She laughed and said, "Oh you mean
looking fat?

00:06:20.521 --> 00:06:33.592
Ryan, you're my son, I love you,
and nothing will every change that."

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:41.112
And it was that moment when I just got it.

00:06:41.112 --> 00:06:43.513
Look, I was more than just a fat kid.

00:06:43.513 --> 00:06:46.653
I was positive, I was cheerful,
I was helpful,

00:06:46.653 --> 00:06:50.263
I might not have had the best physique,
according to society, that is,

00:06:50.263 --> 00:06:52.874
but I have never lacked friends,

00:06:52.874 --> 00:06:58.055
and throughout my life, I have always
had happy people around me.

00:06:58.055 --> 00:07:00.645
However you may look like on the outside,

00:07:00.645 --> 00:07:08.047
it is your character 
that makes you truly shine.

00:07:08.047 --> 00:07:13.445
Ladies and gentlemen, do we love
others just because of looks?

00:07:13.445 --> 00:07:18.356
Don't we love them 
because of who they are deep within?

00:07:18.356 --> 00:07:21.386
Would we stop loving them
if they gained a few pounds,

00:07:21.386 --> 00:07:27.358
developed acne, stopped putting 
on makeup, or cut their hair?

00:07:27.358 --> 00:07:28.878
A famous playwright once wrote,

00:07:28.878 --> 00:07:39.108
"Do I love you because you are beautiful,
or are you beautiful because I love you?"

00:07:39.108 --> 00:07:42.748
These words reflect the idea
that beauty is purely subjective,

00:07:42.748 --> 00:07:45.838
and that it can from appreciation,
not just the other way around.

00:07:45.838 --> 00:07:48.168
We need to educate our children
and grandchildren

00:07:48.168 --> 00:07:51.648
that physical characteristics alone
do not constitute beauty.

00:07:51.648 --> 00:07:54.918
We need to change and we need it now.

00:07:54.918 --> 00:07:57.789
France, Spain, Italy, and Israel
have enacted legislations

00:07:57.789 --> 00:07:59.919
banning overly skinny models.

00:07:59.919 --> 00:08:02.659
Empowering hashtags, such as
"Honor My Curves,"

00:08:02.659 --> 00:08:03.749
"Dare to Wear,"

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.219
and "Celebrate my Size"
has blown up over Instagram.

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:08.660
Body positive movements 
are celebrated everywhere,

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:10.819
and this is a good thing.

00:08:10.819 --> 00:08:13.809
The Body Positive Movement
is a movement that encourages people

00:08:13.809 --> 00:08:16.780
to adopt a more affirming attitude
towards their bodies

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:20.770
with a goal of improving overall
health and fitness.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.910
Because when we are able to live
peacefully inside our own bodies,

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:30.431
only then are we able to care for others
from a point of love and appreciation.

00:08:30.431 --> 00:08:32.371
We need more diverse models
in the media,

00:08:32.371 --> 00:08:35.822
be it in terms of race, height,
body size, skin color,

00:08:35.822 --> 00:08:41.152
be it black or white, brown or yellow, 
red or green, or blue or polka-dotted,

00:08:41.152 --> 00:08:42.431
whatever!

00:08:42.431 --> 00:08:46.052
We need diversity because 
this world is diverse,

00:08:46.052 --> 00:08:47.502
man, people are diverse.

00:08:47.502 --> 00:08:50.373
Don't get me wrong, there is nothing
wrong with being skinny

00:08:50.373 --> 00:08:52.022
or putting on makeup.

00:08:52.022 --> 00:08:55.672
But there is nothing wrong with being
not skinny and not putting on makeup.

00:08:55.672 --> 00:08:59.683
I'll tell you what, if you want to put
on weight, you put on weight.

00:08:59.683 --> 00:09:02.253
If you want to slim down, you slim down.

00:09:02.253 --> 00:09:04.463
If you want to hit the gym,
you hit the gym.

00:09:04.463 --> 00:09:08.252
If you want to put on makeup every day,
you put on makeup every day.

00:09:08.252 --> 00:09:15.734
If you want to dye your hair
in rainbow colors, I don't see why not.

00:09:15.734 --> 00:09:24.635
Be whoever you want to be because
that is who you truly are.

00:09:24.635 --> 00:09:29.985
Beauty is everywhere and inside everyone.

00:09:29.985 --> 00:09:32.566
We may not be able to see 
inner beauty in person,

00:09:32.566 --> 00:09:36.085
but we can definitely feel it.

00:09:36.085 --> 00:09:44.807
I would like to leave you with
these beautiful words by poet Erin Hanson.

00:09:44.807 --> 00:09:48.336
You're made of so much beauty,

00:09:48.336 --> 00:09:52.016
But it seems that you forgot,

00:09:52.016 --> 00:09:55.156
When you decided that you were defined,

00:09:55.156 --> 00:10:00.937
By all the things you're not.

00:10:00.937 --> 00:10:05.225
Whoever they are are, 
whatever they may say,

00:10:05.225 --> 00:10:13.327
be strong, be different, Be-you-tiful.

